maria: Opened PR to consolidate SDK snippets for streaming + retry + pagination across py/ts/go. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4567 — main changes: unify retry backoff (with jitter), add Python async iterator example, add cursor-based pagination examples for TS + Go, and clarify streaming chunk buffer handling.

alex: Do these change the public API or introduce any breaking wording in examples? @maria

maria: No SDK changes — just snippet edits to match the current SDK surface. One small rename in examples only: 'max_retries' -> 'retries' to reflect the SDK arg name. Added a compatibility note in the PR description.

doc-bot: preview: https://docs-preview.redwood.ai/preview/4567 — lint: :white_check_mark: CI: running smoke tests

sam: @maria can you paste the Python streaming snippet here so I can run quick smoke tests against staging?

maria: Sure — Python streaming + retry example I added (async iterator):

```python
from redwood import Client, RetryPolicy

client = Client()
retry = RetryPolicy(retries=3, backoff="exponential", jitter=True)

async for chunk in client.chat.stream("greet", retry=retry):
    print(chunk.text)
```

alex: For TS we should prefer an explicit cursor+limit example for embeddings pagination — helps people implement resume logic. Can you add that?

maria: Added this TS example in the PR: 

```ts
import { Redwood } from "@redwood/inference";

const client = new Redwood();
let cursor: string | null = null;
do {
  const res = await client.embeddings.list({ limit: 100, cursor });
  // process res.items
  cursor = res.nextCursor;
} while (cursor);
```

sam: Go example needs context timeouts and a clearer iterator pattern — here's a suggested snippet I can push to the branch: 

```go
ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(context.Background(), 30*time.Second)
defer cancel()
it := client.Stream(ctx, "chat", opts)
for it.Next() {
    fmt.Println(it.Value().Text)
}
if err := it.Err(); err != nil {
    // handle
}
```

